        <p>APPLETON RIFLE CLUB v. ST. HELENS CIVILIAN RIFLE CLUB. We published recently the results of a match which was fired at St. Helens by teams from the above clubs, the scores being St. Helens 1363 and Appleton 1123. The return match between the two clubs was contested at Appleton Range last Saturday, and again resolted in a win for the St. Helens club, with a total of 543 against 493 by their opponents. Contrary to expecta- tions, after the previous wet weather experienced, the day proved an ideal one for shooting. The total scores for both matches were : St. Helens, 1,006 ; Appleton, 1,620, giving a majority of 286 for the former. It should be stated that in the former match, decimal scoring was used, whereas in the latter N.R.A. scoring was adopted. The conditions last Saturday were : Each team to consist of ten members, the best eight scores to count ; distance 100 yards. (A) 7 shots, last year's N.R.A. Standard Target. Z inch bull. (B) 7 shots, this year's N.R.A. Standard Target. 3 inch bull. (C) 7 shots, disappearing figure Target. Highest possible score, 91. The following were the aggregate scores : St. llelens C. IL C. F. Smith 76 F. .7. West J. Menzies 11. 13. West 11. Hyde 'l'. W. Mather 63 j. Hayes J. 11. Fearnley</p>
